  "documentation": {
    "range": "This species is distributed in the western Pacific from Sabah, Malaysia to Indonesia (northeastern Kalimantan and Bali), the Ryukyu Islands of Japan, the Philippines, Papua New Guinea south to the Great Barrier Reef of Australia, New Caledonia,&#160;Christmas Island, Micronesia and the Cook Islands (Allen and Erdmann 2012, Hui&#160;<em>et al.</em>&#160;2014, Koeda <em>et al.</em>&#160;2014). It occurs from 1-50 metres depth (Allen and Erdmann 2012).",
    "population": "Population data are limited.",
    "habitats": "This species inhabits outer coral and rocky reefs and steep slopes with caves. The maximum total length is 10 cm (Allen and Erdmann 2012).",
    "threats": "There are no known major threats.",
    "measures": "There are no species-specific conservation actions.",
    "use_trade": "Some species in the family Anomalopidae are used in public aquariums and are sometimes targeted by local fishers for bait (Paxton and Johnson 2002).",
    "rationale": "This widely distributed, reef-associated species has no known major threats; therefore, it is listed as Least Concern.",
